, and performance.","zh":"Accelint-ts-testing是一个用于Accelint系统家族的Web标准库","ja":"Accelint-ts-testingはAccelintシステムファミリーのためのWeb標準ライブラリです","ko":"Accelint-ts-testing은 Accelint 시스템 패밀리의 Web 표준 라이브러리입니다","es":"Accelint-ts-testing es una biblioteca de pruebas para la familia de sistemas Accelint que utiliza Vitest","fr":"Accelint-ts-testing est une bibliothèque de tests pour la famille de systèmes Accelint qui utilise Vitest","de":"Accelint-ts-testing ist eine Testbibliothek für die Accelint-Systemfamilie, die Vitest verwendet","pt":"O que é Accelint-ts-testing? É uma biblioteca de testes para a família de sistemas Accelint, focada em testes Vitest.","ru":"Что такое Accelint-ts-testing? Это библиотека тестирования для семейства систем Accelint, ориентированная на тесты Vitest с помощью ИИ Агентов","ar":"ما هي Accelint-ts-testing؟ هي مكتبة اختبارات للعائلة من أنظمة Accelint، تركز على اختبارات Vitest مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"},"features":{"en":["Provides Vitest best practices for writing maintainable tests","Guides on proper global mock cleanup configuration to avoid non-deterministic failures","Offers expert-level guidance on test organization and clarity","Helps prevent ''action at a distance'' failures by ensuring proper mock cleanup","Supports effective test performance optimization"],"zh":["Vitest测试的最佳实践","测试组织和清晰度的指导","性能优化的专家级建议","NEVER跳过全局模拟清理配置","避免手动清理导致的非确定性失败"],"ja":["Vitestテストのベストプラクティス","テストの組織と明確性のガイド","パフォーマンスの最適化の専門家レベルのアドバイス","NEVERグローバルモックのクリーンアップ構成をスキップ","手動のクリーンアップによる非決定性の失敗を避ける"],"ko":["Vitest 테스트의 모범 사례","테스트의 구성과 명확성에 대한 가이드","성능 최적화의 전문가 수준의 제안","NEVER 전역 모의 정리 구성跳过","수동 정리 때문에 발생하는 비결정성 실패를 피하는"],"es":["Proporciona patrones para pruebas de Vitest mantenibles y efectivas","Incluye recomendaciones para la organización de pruebas","Ofrece orientación para la claridad y el rendimiento de las pruebas","Evita la configuración de limpieza de mocks globales","Permite la escritura de pruebas de Vitest expertas"],"fr":["Fournit des modèles pour des tests Vitest maintenables et efficaces","Inclut des recommandations pour l''organisation des tests","Offre des conseils pour la clarté et les performances des tests","Évite la configuration de nettoyage de mocks globaux","Permet l''écriture de tests Vitest experts"],"de":["Bietet Muster für wartbare und effektive Vitest-Tests","Enthält Empfehlungen für die Organisation von Tests","Bietet Leitfäden für die Klarheit und Leistung von Tests","Vermeidet die Konfiguration der globalen Mock-Reinigung","Ermöglicht das Schreiben von Experten-Vitest-Tests"],"pt":["Padrões abrangentes para testes Vitest","Evita falhas não determinísticas com configuração de limpeza de mocks","Melhores práticas para organização de testes","Otimização de desempenho para testes Vitest","Integração com a família de sistemas Accelint"],"ru":["Комплексные шаблоны для тестов Vitest","Избежание недетерминированных сбоев с помощью конфигурации очистки моков","Лучшие практики для организации тестов","Оптимизация производительности для тестов Vitest","Интеграция с семейством систем Accelint с помощью ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["أنماط شاملة لاختبارات Vitest","تجنب الفشل غير المحدد مع إعداد تنظيف المॉक","أفضل الممارسات لتخطيط الاختبارات","تحسين الأداء لاختبارات Vitest","التكامل مع عائلة أنظمة Accelint مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use accelint-ts-testing","what is accelint-ts-testing","accelint-ts-testing vs Jest","accelint-ts-testing install guide","Vitest best practices for AI agents","accelint-ts-testing setup for developers","accelint-ts-testing alternative testing frameworks","accelint-ts-testing tutorial for beginners","accelint-ts-testing and Vitest integration"],"zh":["Accelint-ts-testing","Vitest测试","AI工具","Web标准库","测试组织","性能优化","NEVER跳过全局模拟清理配置"],"ja":["Accelint-ts-testing","Vitestテスト","AIエージェント","Web標準ライブラリ","テストの組織","パフォーマンスの最適化","NEVERグローバルモックのクリーンアップ構成をスキップ"],"ko":["Accelint-ts-testing","Vitest 테스트","AI 에이전트","Web 표준 라이브러리","테스트의 구성","성능 최적화","NEVER 전역 모의 정리 구성跳过"],"es":["accelint-ts-testing","pruebas de Vitest","biblioteca estándar web","pruebas mantenibles","pruebas efectivas","organización de pruebas","claridad de pruebas","rendimiento de pruebas","Vitest para desarrolladores"],"fr":["accelint-ts-testing","tests Vitest","bibliothèque web standard","tests maintenables","tests efficaces","organisation des tests","clarté des tests","performances des tests","Vitest pour développeurs"],"de":["accelint-ts-testing","Vitest-Tests","Web-Standardbibliothek","wartbare Tests","effektive Tests","Testorganisation","Testklarheit","Testleistung","Vitest für Entwickler"],"pt":["Accelint-ts-testing","testes Vitest","biblioteca de testes","melhores práticas para testes","evitar falhas não determinísticas","configuração de limpeza de mocks","otimização de desempenho para testes"],"ru":["Accelint-ts-testing","тесты Vitest","библиотека тестирования","лучшие практики для тестирования","избежание недетерминированных сбоев","конфигурация очистки моков","оптимизация производительности для тестов","ИИ Агенты"],"ar":["Accelint-ts-testing","اختبارات Vitest","مكتبة اختبارات","أفضل الممارسات للاختبارات","تجنب الفشل غير المحدد","إعداد تنظيف المॉक","تحسين الأداء للاختبارات","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"gohypergiant","repo":"standard-toolkit","repoPath":"gohypergiant/standard-toolkit","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.325Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"accelint-ts-testing","description":"Comprehensive vitest testing guidance for TypeScript projects. Use when (1) Writing new tests with AAA pattern, parameterized tests, or async/await, (2) Reviewing test code for anti-patterns like loose assertions (toBeTruthy), over-mocking, or nested describe blocks, (3) Optimizing slow test suites, (4) Implementing property-based testing with fast-check - especially for encode/decode pairs, roundtrip properties, validators, normalizers, and idempotence checks. Covers test organization, assertions, test doubles hierarchy (fakes/stubs/mocks), async testing, performance patterns, and property-based testing patterns. Trigger keywords on vitest, *.test.ts, describe, it, expect, vi.mock, fast-check, fc.property, roundtrip, idempotence.","version":"3.0","bodyPreview":"# Vitest Best Practices\n\nComprehensive patterns for writing maintainable, effective vitest tests. Focused on expert-level guidance for test organization, clarity, and performance.\n\n## NEVER Do When Writing Vitest Tests\n\n- **NEVER skip global mock cleanup configuration** - Manual cleanup appears safe but creates \"action at a distance\" failures: a mock in test file A leaks into test file B running 3 files later, causing non-deterministic failures that only appear when tests run in specific orders.","body":"# Vitest Best Practices\n\nComprehensive patterns for writing maintainable, effective vitest tests. Focused on expert-level guidance for test organization, clarity, and performance.\n\n## NEVER Do When Writing Vitest Tests\n\n- **NEVER skip global mock cleanup configuration** - Manual cleanup appears safe but creates \"action at a distance\" failures: a mock in test file A leaks into test file B running 3 files later, causing non-deterministic failures that only appear when tests run in specific orders. These Heisenbugs waste hours in CI debugging. Configure `clearMocks: true`, `mockReset: true`, `restoreMocks: true` in `vitest.config.ts` once to eliminate this entire class of order-dependent failure.\n- **NEVER nest describe blocks more than 2 levels deep** - Deep nesting creates cognitive overhead and excessive indentation. Put context in test names instead: `it(''should add item to empty cart'')` vs `describe(''when cart is empty'', () => describe(''addItem'', ...))`.\n- **NEVER write test descriptions that don''t read as sentences** - Test descriptions must complete the sentence \"it ...\" in lowercase. Write `it(''should add item to cart'')` not `it(''Add item to cart'')` or `it(''It should add item to cart'')`. The description reads as a sentence when prefixed with \"it\": \"it should add item to cart\". Capitalized starts, non-sentence formats like `it(''addToCart test'')`, or redundant \"It should\" break readability and test output consistency. Example-based tests use `it(''should...'')` while property-based tests use `it(''property: ...'')` format.\n- **NEVER test library internals that the library already tests** - Testing `expect(array.map(fn)).toEqual(expected)` wastes time verifying that Array.prototype.map works correctly. The JavaScript/TypeScript standard library and established third-party libraries are already well-tested. Focus tests on your business logic, not on proving that lodash, React, or the language itself works. If you find yourself testing \"does this library function do what it claims?\", you''re testing the wrong layer. Test how your code uses libraries, not whether libraries work.\n- **NEVER export internal functions just to test them** - Tests should verify behavior through the public API, not reach into implementation details. Exporting private helpers, internal utilities, or implementation functions solely to enable testing is a code smell that indicates either: (1) the public API is insufficient for testing the behavior, or (2) the tests are verifying implementation details instead of behavior. If internal logic is complex enough to warrant dedicated testing, extract it into a separate module with its own public API and test file. Private functions get tested indirectly through the public functions that call them.\n- **NEVER mock your own pure functions** - Mocking internal code makes tests brittle and less valuable. Mock only external dependencies (APIs, databases, third-party libraries). Prefer fakes > stubs > spies > mocks.\n- **NEVER use loose assertions like `toBeTruthy()` or `toBeDefined()`** - These assertions pass for multiple distinct values you never intended: `toBeTruthy()` passes for `1`, `\"false\"`, `[]`, and `{}` - all semantically different. When refactoring changes `getUser()` from returning `{id: 1}` to returning `1`, your test still passes but your production code breaks. Loose assertions create false confidence that evaporates in production. `toBeTypeOf()` is NOT a loose assertion.\n- **NEVER test implementation details instead of behavior** - Tests that verify \"function X was called 3 times\" create false failures: you optimize code to call X once via memoization, all tests fail, yet the user experience is identical (and faster). These tests actively punish performance improvements and refactoring. Test what users observe (outputs given inputs), not how your code achieves it internally.\n- **NEVER share mutable state between tests** - Tests that depend on execution order or previous test state create flaky, unreliable suites. Each test must be fully independent with fresh setup.\n- **NEVER use `any` or skip type checking in test files** - When implementation signatures change, tests with `as any` silently pass while calling functions with wrong arguments. You ship broken code that TypeScript could have caught. Tests are executable documentation: `user as any` communicates nothing, but `createTestUser(Partial<User>)` shows exactly what properties matter for this test case.\n- **NEVER assume TypeScript types prevent runtime errors** - TS types are compile-time only and vanish at runtime. Testing only \"type-valid\" inputs creates a false sense of security. In production, functions receive invalid data from JSON APIs without validation, `JSON.parse()` results, external libraries, user input, and database records. A function typed as `process(data: ValidData)` can still receive `null`, `undefined`, or malformed objects at runtime. Test defensive programming scenarios: pass `null` to non-nullable parameters, `undefined` to required fields, malformed objects to typed parameters. These \"type-invalid\" tests catch real bugs that TypeScript cannot prevent.\n- **NEVER write weak properties when stronger ones exist** - Property-based tests that only verify \"no exception thrown\" or \"returns a value\" provide minimal coverage. When testing encode/decode pairs, verify roundtrip equality (`decode(encode(x)) === x`), not just that decode succeeds. When testing normalization, verify idempotence (`normalize(normalize(x)) === normalize(x)`), not just that it returns a string. Weak properties give false confidence: they pass but don''t actually validate correctness.\n\n## Before Writing Tests, Ask\n\nApply these expert thinking patterns before implementing tests:\n\n### Test Isolation and Setup\n- **Where should cleanup logic live?** Think in layers: configuration eliminates entire error classes (mock cleanup in vitest.config.ts), setup files handle project-wide concerns (custom matchers, global mocks), beforeEach handles test-specific state. Each test doing its own mock cleanup is like each function doing its own null checks - it works but misses the point. Push concerns to the highest appropriate layer.\n- **Does this test depend on previous tests or shared state?** Test suites are parallel universes - each test should work identically whether it runs first, last, or alone. State dependency creates \"quantum tests\" that pass or fail based on execution order. If a test needs data from another test, they''re actually one test split artificially.\n\n### What to Test\n- **Am I testing behavior or implementation?** Test what users experience (inputs → outputs), not how code achieves it (which functions were called). Implementation tests break during safe refactoring.\n- **What''s the simplest dependency I can use?** Real implementation > fake > stub > spy > mock. Each step down this hierarchy adds brittleness. Mock only when using real code is impractical (external APIs, slow operations).\n\n### Test Clarity\n- **Can someone understand this test in 5 seconds?** Follow AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert) with clear boundaries. If setup is complex, extract to helper functions with descriptive names.\n- **Are there multiple variations of the same behavior?** Use `it.each()` for parameterized tests instead of copying test structure. One assertion per concept keeps tests focused.\n\n### Performance and Maintenance\n- **Will this test still be valuable in 6 months?** Avoid testing framework internals or trivial operations. Focus on business logic, edge cases, and error handling that actually prevent bugs.\n- **Is this test fast enough to run on every save?** Avoid expensive operations in tests. Use fakes for databases, mock timers for delays, stub external calls. Tests should complete in milliseconds.\n\n## What This Skill Covers\n\nExpert guidance on vitest testing patterns:\n\n1. **Organization** - File placement, naming, describe block structure\n2. **AAA Pattern** - Arrange, Act, Assert for instant clarity\n3. **Parameterized Tests** - Using `it.each()` to reduce duplication\n4. **Error Handling** - Testing exceptions, edge cases, fault injection\n5. **Assertions** - Strict assertions to catch unintended values\n6. **Test Doubles** - Fakes, stubs, mocks, spies hierarchy and when to use each\n7. **Async Testing** - Promises, async/await, timers, concurrent tests\n8. **Performance** - Fast tests through efficient setup and global config\n9. **Vitest Features** - Coverage, watch mode, setup files, config discovery\n10. **Snapshot Testing** - When snapshots help vs hurt maintainability\n11. **Property-Based Testing** - Using fast-check for stronger coverage with generated inputs\n\n## How to Use\n\nThis skill uses a **progressive disclosure** structure to minimize context usage:\n\n### 1. Start with the Overview (AGENTS.md)\nRead [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for a concise overview of all rules with one-line summaries and the workflow for discovering existing test configuration.\n\n### 2. Check for Existing Test Configuration\nBefore writing tests:\n- First check `vitest.config.ts` for global mock cleanup settings (`clearMocks`, `mockReset`, `restoreMocks`)\n- Then search for setup files (`test/setup.ts`, `vitest.setup.ts`, etc.) and analyze their configuration\n- See the workflow in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md#workflow-before-writing-tests)\n\n### 3. Load Specific Rules as Needed\nUse these explicit triggers to know when to load each reference file:\n\n**MANDATORY Loading (load entire file):**\n- **Writing async tests with promises/timers** → [async-testing.md](references/async-testing.md)\n- **Working with mocks, stubs, spies, or fakes** → [test-doubles.md](references/test-doubles.md)\n- **Auditing/reviewing existing test files** → [property-based-testing.md](references/property-based-testing.md) (to identify PBT opportunities)\n\n**Load When You See These Patterns:**\n- **Nested describe blocks >2 levels deep** → [organization.md](references/organization.md)\n- **Test files not co-located with implementation** → [organization.md](references/organization.md)\n- **Tests without clear Arrange/Act/Assert structure** → [aaa-pattern.md](references/aaa-pattern.md)\n- **Duplicate test code with slight variations** → [parameterized-tests.md](references/parameterized-tests.md)\n- **Missing error case tests or inadequate edge case coverage** → [error-handling.md](references/error-handling.md)\n- **Loose assertions like `toBeTruthy()` or `toBeDefined()`** → [assertions.md](references/assertions.md)\n- **Tests running slow (>100ms per test)** → [performance.md](references/performance.md)\n- **Need coverage, watch mode, or vitest-specific features** → [vitest-features.md](references/vitest-features.md)\n- **Considering or reviewing snapshot tests** → [snapshot-testing.md](references/snapshot-testing.md)\n- **Encode/decode pairs, validators, normalizers, or pure functions** → [property-based-testing.md](references/property-based-testing.md)\n- **Code with invariants, mathematical properties, or data transformations** → [property-based-testing.md](references/property-based-testing.md)\n- **Existing fast-check or property-based tests** → [property-based-testing.md](references/property-based-testing.md)\n\n**Do NOT Load Unless Specifically Needed:**\n- Do NOT load [performance.md](references/performance.md) if tests are fast (<50ms)\n- Do NOT load [snapshot-testing.md](references/snapshot-testing.md) unless snapshots are mentioned\n- Do NOT load [vitest-features.md](references/vitest-features.md) for basic test writing\n\n### 4. Apply the Pattern\nEach reference file contains:\n- ❌ Incorrect examples showing the anti-pattern\n- ✅ Correct examples showing the optimal implementation\n- Explanations of why the pattern matters\n\n### 5. Use the Report Template\nWhen this skill is invoked for test code review, use the standardized report format:\n\n**Template:** [`assets/output-report-template.md`](assets/output-report-template.md)\n\nThe report format provides:\n- Executive Summary with test quality impact assessment\n- Severity levels (Critical, High, Medium, Low) for prioritization\n- Impact analysis (test reliability, maintainability, performance, clarity)\n- Categorization (Test Organization, Assertions, Test Doubles, Async Testing, Performance)\n- Pattern references linking to detailed guidance in references/\n- Summary table for tracking all issues\n\n**When to use the report template:**\n- Skill invoked directly via `/accelint-ts-testing <path>`\n- User asks to \"review test code\" or \"audit tests\" across file(s), invoking skill implicitly\n\n**When NOT to use the report template:**\n- User asks to \"write a test for this function\" (direct implementation)\n- User asks \"what''s wrong with this test?\" (answer the question)\n- User requests specific test fixes (apply fixes directly without formal report)\n\n**IMPORTANT: When auditing tests, ALWAYS check for property-based testing opportunities**\n- Load [property-based-testing.md](references/property-based-testing.md) during every audit\n- Follow the \"Workflow: Test Code Review/Audit\" in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md)\n- Check for high-value PBT patterns: encode/decode pairs, normalizers, validators, pure functions, sorting functions\n- Include PBT opportunities in the audit report even if no other issues are found\n\n## Quick Example\n\nSee [quick-start.md](references/quick-start.md) for a complete before/after example showing how this skill transforms unclear tests into clear, maintainable ones.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:03:01.887Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for JavaScript Testing Agents needing comprehensive Vitest test organization and performance optimization.","zh":"非常适合需要全面 Vitest 测试组织和性能优化的 JavaScript 测试代理。","ja":"JavaScript テストエージェントが包括的な Vitest テストの組織化とパフォーマンスの最適化を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"포괄적인 Vitest 테스트 조직 및 성능 최적화가 필요한 JavaScript 테스트 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de prueba de JavaScript que necesitan una organización y optimización de rendimiento de pruebas de Vitest integral.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de test JavaScript nécessitant une organisation et une optimisation des performances de test de Vitest complètes.","de":"Perfekt für JavaScript-Testagenten, die eine umfassende Vitest-Testorganisation und Leistungsoptimierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Teste JavaScript que necessitam de organização de testes Vitest abrangente e otimização de desempenho.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов тестирования JavaScript, которым требуется комплексная организация тестов Vitest и оптимизация производительности.","ar":"مثالي لعميل اختبار جافا سكريبت الذي يحتاج إلى تنظيم اختبار فيتست شاملة وتحسين الأداء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write maintainable and effective Vitest tests with expert-level guidance on test organization, clarity, and performance, utilizing best practices such as global mock cleanup configuration to prevent non-deterministic failures.","zh":"赋予代理编写可维护和有效的 Vitest 测试的能力，利用全球模拟清理配置等最佳实践，提供专家级的测试组织、清晰度和性能指导，以防止非确定性失败。","ja":"エージェントが保守可能で効果的な Vitest テストを記述できるようにすることで、テストの組織化、明確さ、パフォーマンスに関する専門家レベルの指導を提供し、グローバルモッククリーンナップ構成などのベストプラクティスを活用して非決定性の失敗を防ぎます。","ko":"전역 모의 정리 구성과 같은 모범 사례를 사용하여 전문가 수준의 테스트 조직, 명확성 및 성능 지침을 제공하고, 비결정적 오류를 방지하여 에이전트가 유지 관리 가능하고 효과적인 Vitest 테스트를 작성할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas de Vitest mantenibles y efectivas con orientación de experto sobre organización de pruebas, claridad y rendimiento, utilizando las mejores prácticas como la configuración de limpieza de mock global para prevenir fallos no determinísticos.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des tests Vitest maintenables et efficaces avec une orientation d''expert sur l''organisation des tests, la clarté et les performances, en utilisant les meilleures pratiques telles que la configuration de nettoyage de mock global pour prévenir les défaillances non déterministes.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Vitest-Tests zu schreiben, die wartbar und effektiv sind, mit Expertenratgeber zu Testorganisation, Klarheit und Leistung, unter Nutzung von Best Practices wie globaler Mock-Reinigungskonfiguration, um nichtdeterministische Ausfälle zu verhindern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever testes Vitest mantidos e eficazes com orientação de nível de especialista sobre organização de testes, clareza e desempenho, utilizando as melhores práticas, como configuração de limpeza de mock global para prevenir falhas não determinísticas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать поддерживаемые и эффективные тесты Vitest с экспертным уровнем руководства по организации тестов, ясности и производительности, используя лучшие практики, такие как глобальная конфигурация очистки mock для предотвращения недетерминированных сбоев.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من كتابة اختبارات فيتست مدعومة وفعالة مع إرشادات على مستوى الخبراء حول تنظيم الاختبارات والوضوح والأداء، باستخدام أفضل الممارسات مثل تكوين تنظيف العرض العالمي لمنع الفشل غير القابل للتحديد."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating test organization for large-scale JavaScript projects","Generating high-performance Vitest tests with optimized configuration","Debugging non-deterministic test failures caused by mock leaks"],"zh":["为大型 JavaScript 项目自动化测试组织","使用优化的配置生成高性能 Vitest 测试","调试由模拟泄漏引起的非确定性测试失败"],"ja":["大規模な JavaScript プロジェクトのテスト組織の自動化","最適化された構成を使用して高パフォーマンスの Vitest テストを生成する","モック漏れによって引き起こされる非決定性テストの失敗をデバッグする"],"ko":["대규모 JavaScript 프로젝트의 테스트 조직 자동화","최적화된 구성으로 높은 성능의 Vitest 테스트 생성","모의 누수로 인한 비결정적 테스트 실패 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de la organización de pruebas para proyectos JavaScript a gran escala","Generación de pruebas de Vitest de alto rendimiento con configuración optimizada","Depuración de fallos de prueba no determinísticos causados por fugas de mock"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''organisation des tests pour les projets JavaScript à grande échelle","Génération de tests Vitest de haute performance avec configuration optimisée","Débogage des défaillances de test non déterministes causées par des fuites de mock"],"de":["Automatisierung der Testorganisation für groß angelegte JavaScript-Projekte","Generierung von Vitest-Tests mit hoher Leistung und optimierter Konfiguration","Fehlerbehebung bei nichtdeterministischen Testfehlern, die durch Mock-Lecks verursacht werden"],"pt":["Automatizar a organização de testes para projetos JavaScript de grande escala","Gerar testes Vitest de alto desempenho com configuração otimizada","Depurar falhas de testes não determinísticas causadas por vazamentos de mock"],"ru":["Автоматизировать организацию тестов для крупномасштабных проектов JavaScript","Генерировать высокопроизводительные тесты Vitest с оптимизированной конфигурацией","Отлаживать недетерминированные сбои тестов, вызванные утечками mock"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي في تنظيم الاختبارات لمشاريع جافا سكريبت واسعة النطاق","γενرار اختبارات فيتست عالية الأداء مع تكوين محسن","تصحيح أخطاء الاختبارات غير القابلة للتحديد الناجمة عن تسربات العرض"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Vitest testing framework","JavaScript and TypeScript compatibility only"],"zh":["需要 Vitest 测试框架","仅与 JavaScript 和 TypeScript 兼容"],"ja":["Vitest テスト フレームワークが必要","JavaScript と TypeScript との互換性のみ"],"ko":["Vitest 테스트 프레임워크 필요","JavaScript 및 TypeScript와의 호환성만"],"es":["Requiere el marco de pruebas de Vitest","Compatibilidad solo con JavaScript y TypeScript"],"fr":["Nécessite le framework de test Vitest","Compatibilité uniquement avec JavaScript et TypeScript"],"de":["Erfordert das Vitest-Testframework","Kompatibilität nur mit JavaScript und TypeScript"],"pt":["Exige o framework de teste Vitest","Compatibilidade apenas com JavaScript e TypeScript"],"ru":["Требует тестового фреймворка Vitest","Совместимость только с JavaScript и TypeScript"],"ar":["يتطلب إطار اختبار فيتست","متوافق مع جافا سكريبت و타입سكريبت فقط"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"3e01b52f50108c3caf57a7ca6ef19fdcf55a0393b1f1b1398df7287dedcdd41b","qualityScore":40}');
