r":["تتبع أخطاء JavaScript","مراقبة الأداء","تقارير أخطاء مفصلة","التكامل مع Django و Python","دعم تقارير الحوادث وتقرير CSP"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Sentry JavaScript 错误追踪","如何使用Sentry","什么是错误追踪","Sentry替代品","Sentry vs Bugsnag","Sentry安装","Sentry设置指南"],"ja":["Sentry JavaScript エラー追跡","Sentryの使い方","エラートラッキングとは","Sentryの代替","Sentry vs Bugsnag","Sentryのインストール","Sentryの設定ガイド"],"ko":["Sentry JavaScript 버그 추적","Sentry 사용법","오류 추적이란","Sentry 대체","Sentry vs Bugsnag","Sentry 설치","Sentry 설정 가이드"],"es":["herramientas de seguimiento de errores","monitoreo de rendimiento","Sentry alternativa","cómo usar Sentry","guía de instalación de Sentry","Sentry vs New Relic","seguimiento de errores en JavaScript","monitoreo de aplicaciones web"],"fr":["outils de suivi d''erreurs","surveillance des performances","alternative à Sentry","comment utiliser Sentry","guide d''installation de Sentry","Sentry vs New Relic","suivi d''erreurs en JavaScript","surveillance d''applications web"],"de":["Fehler-Tracking-Tools","Leistungsüberwachung","Sentry-Alternative","wie man Sentry verwendet","Sentry-Installationsanleitung","Sentry vs New Relic","Fehlerverfolgung in JavaScript","Anwendungsüberwachung"],"pt":["como usar Sentry","o que é Sentry","Sentry vs New Relic","Sentry alternative","instalar Sentry","guia de configuração do Sentry","monitoramento de desempenho JavaScript","rastreamento de erros JavaScript"],"ru":["как использовать Sentry","что такое Sentry","Sentry vs New Relic","альтернатива Sentry","установить Sentry","руководство по настройке Sentry","мониторинг производительности JavaScript","отслеживание ошибок JavaScript"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Sentry","ما هي Sentry","Sentry مقابل New Relic","بديل Sentry","تثبيت Sentry","دليل إعداد Sentry","مراقبة الأداء JavaScript","تتبع أخطاء JavaScript"]}},"owner":"getsentry","repo":"sentry","repoPath":"getsentry/sentry","stars":43215,"forks":4613,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T01:51:48Z","topics":["apm","crash-reporting","crash-reports","csp-report","devops","django","error-logging","error-monitoring","fair-source","hacktoberfest","monitor","monitoring","python","sentry","tag-production"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"sentry-javascript-bugs","description":"Sentry JavaScript frontend bug pattern review based on real production errors. Use when reviewing React/TypeScript frontend code for common bug patterns. Trigger keywords: javascript bug review, frontend errors, react error patterns, sentry frontend bugs.","bodyPreview":"# Sentry JavaScript Frontend Bug Pattern Review\n\nFind bugs in Sentry frontend code by checking for the patterns that cause real production errors.\n\nThis skill encodes patterns from 428 real production issues (201 resolved, 130 ignored, 97 unresolved) generating over 524,000 error events across 93,000+ affected users. These are not theoretical risks -- they are the actual bugs that ship most often, with known fixes from resolved issues.\n\n## Scope\n\nYou receive scoped code chunks from Warden''s diff","body":"# Sentry JavaScript Frontend Bug Pattern Review\n\nFind bugs in Sentry frontend code by checking for the patterns that cause real production errors.\n\nThis skill encodes patterns from 428 real production issues (201 resolved, 130 ignored, 97 unresolved) generating over 524,000 error events across 93,000+ affected users. These are not theoretical risks -- they are the actual bugs that ship most often, with known fixes from resolved issues.\n\n## Scope\n\nYou receive scoped code chunks from Warden''s diff pipeline. Each chunk is a changed hunk (or coalesced group of nearby hunks) with surrounding context.\n\n1. Analyze the chunk against the pattern checks below.\n2. Use `Read` and `Grep` to trace data flow beyond the chunk when needed — follow component props, hook return values, API response shapes.\n3. Report only **HIGH** and **MEDIUM** confidence findings.\n\n| Confidence | Criteria                                                              | Action                       |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| **HIGH**   | Traced the code path, confirmed the pattern matches a known bug class | Report with fix              |\n| **MEDIUM** | Pattern is present but context may mitigate it                        | Report as needs verification |\n| **LOW**    | Theoretical or mitigated elsewhere                                    | Do not report                |\n\n## Step 1: Classify the Code\n\nDetermine what you are reviewing and load the relevant reference.\n\n| Code Type                                                               | Load Reference                                               |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Null/undefined property access, optional chaining, object destructuring | `${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT}/references/null-reference-errors.md`   |\n| Dashboard widgets, chart visualization, widget URL generation           | `${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT}/references/dashboard-widget-errors.md` |\n| Trace views, span details, trace tree rendering                         | `${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT}/references/trace-view-errors.md`       |\n| API calls, response handling, error states, fetch wrappers              | `${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT}/references/api-response-handling.md`   |\n| React hooks, context providers, render loops, component lifecycle       | `${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT}/references/react-lifecycle-errors.md`  |\n| AI Insights, LLM prompt parsing, gen_ai span data                       | `${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT}/references/ai-insights-parsing.md`     |\n| Array operations, date/time values, numeric formatting                  | `${CLAUDE_SKILL_ROOT}/references/range-and-bounds-errors.md` |\n\nIf the code spans multiple categories, load all relevant references.\n\n## Step 2: Check for Top Bug Patterns\n\nThese are ordered by combined frequency and impact from real production data.\n\n### Check 1: Null/Undefined Property Access -- 158 issues, 46,337 events\n\nCode accesses a property on a value that may be null or undefined. This is the single most common bug pattern in the Sentry frontend.\n\n**Red flags:**\n\n- Accessing `.id`, `.slug`, `.name`, `.type`, `.match`, `.length`, `.charCodeAt` without null checks\n- Using `object.property` instead of `object?.property` on data from API responses\n- Passing API response data directly to utility functions without null validation\n- Accessing DOM element properties from `querySelector` or `useRef` without checking if the element exists\n- Destructuring objects from hooks/stores that may return null during loading states\n- Calling `.dispatchEvent()` on elements that have been unmounted\n\n**Safe patterns:**\n\n- Optional chaining: `obj?.property?.nested`\n- Default values: `const value = obj?.field ?? defaultValue`\n- Null guards before function calls: `if (data) { parser.parse(data); }`\n- Early returns for null/undefined parameters in utility functions\n\n### Check 2: Dashboard Widget Input Validation -- 6 issues, 90,482 events\n\nWidget visualization components throw when receiving data in unexpected formats.\n\n**Red flags:**\n\n- Rendering chart components without checking if data contains plottable values\n- Calling `getWidgetExploreUrl()` for widget types that do not support multiple queries\n- Passing undefined `field` values to `parseFunction()` or similar field parsers\n- Not handling empty API responses in widget data fetchers\n\n**Safe patterns:**\n\n- Validate data shape before rendering: `if (!hasPlottableValues(data)) return <EmptyState />`\n- Check widget query count before generating explore URLs\n- Guard field parsers: `if (!field) return null`\n\n### Check 3: Trace View Data Integrity -- 12 issues, 328,482 events\n\nThe trace tree renderer and trace detail views encounter data that violates structural assumptions.\n\n**Red flags:**\n\n- Building trace trees without cycle detection (or detecting cycles but not handling them gracefully)\n- Looking up projects by ID from span data without checking if the project is accessible\n- Generating trace links without validating `traceSlug` is non-empty\n- Using `captureException` in render paths without deduplication (fires every render cycle)\n\n**Safe patterns:**\n\n- Break cycles by detaching cyclic nodes as orphan roots\n- Validate traceSlug before generating links: `if (!traceSlug) return fallbackLink`\n- Deduplicate error captures using a ref: `if (!capturedRef.current) { captureException(...); capturedRef.current = true; }`\n- Check project access before rendering span details\n\n### Check 4: API Response Shape Assumptions -- 31 issues, 24,019 events\n\nFrontend code assumes API responses have a specific shape but the response is empty, undefined, or has an unexpected status code.\n\n**Red flags:**\n\n- Not handling 200 responses with empty bodies (e.g., `GET /customers/{orgSlug}/` returns 200 with no body)\n- Not handling 402 (Payment Required) status codes in subscription flows\n- Not handling 409 (Conflict) status codes in mutation endpoints\n- Treating `UndefinedResponseBodyError` as unexpected (it indicates the API returned no parseable body)\n- Assuming SelectAsync options will always load successfully\n\n**Safe patterns:**\n\n- Check response body before parsing: `if (!response.body) return null`\n- Handle specific 4xx status codes in catch blocks\n- Provide fallback empty states for failed API fetches instead of throwing\n\n### Check 5: React Lifecycle Violations -- 10 issues, 2,595 events\n\nComponents violate React rendering rules, causing infinite loops or crashes.\n\n**Red flags:**\n\n- Setting state unconditionally in `useEffect` without proper dependency arrays\n- Calling `useOrganization()` in components that render before organization context is loaded\n- Using `useContext()` outside the provider boundary\n- Passing objects as React children instead of strings/elements\n- Components that trigger immediate re-render on mount\n\n**Safe patterns:**\n\n- Always provide dependency arrays for `useEffect`\n- Guard context hooks: `const org = useOrganization(); if (!org) return <Loading />`\n- Wrap organization-dependent routes in a provider boundary\n- Validate element types before rendering: `if (typeof Component !== ''function'') return null`\n\n### Check 6: AI Insights Data Parsing -- 2 issues, 3,005 events\n\nJSON parsing of AI prompt messages and gen_ai span data fails on non-standard formats.\n\n**Red flags:**\n\n- Calling `JSON.parse()` on `ai.prompt.messages` span attributes without try-catch\n- Assuming all AI model responses produce valid JSON\n- Not handling the \"parts\" format for multi-modal AI messages\n\n**Safe patterns:**\n\n- Wrap all `JSON.parse` calls on external data in try-catch\n- Check for leading `[` or `{` before parsing\n- Provide raw-text fallback rendering when parsing fails\n\n### Check 7: Array and Bounds Validation -- 15 issues, 3,120 events\n\nArray operations and numeric formatting with values that exceed valid ranges.\n\n**Red flags:**\n\n- Using `result.push(...largeArray)` (crashes when array is too large)\n- Passing unclamped values to `toLocaleString({maximumFractionDigits: n})`\n- Constructing Date objects from unvalidated timestamps\n- Recursive component rendering without depth limits\n\n**Safe patterns:**\n\n- Use `concat` or iterative push for potentially large arrays\n- Clamp numeric format parameters: `Math.min(100, Math.max(0, precision))`\n- Validate dates before constructing: `if (isNaN(new Date(ts).getTime())) return fallback`\n- Use iterative rendering with explicit stacks for deeply nested structures\n\n### Check 8: Logic Correctness -- not pattern-based\n\nAfter checking all known patterns above, reason about the changed code itself:\n\n- Does every code path return the correct type (or JSX)?\n- Are all branches of conditionals handled (especially missing `else` / default cases in switches)?\n- Can any prop or state value (null, undefined, empty array, empty string) cause unexpected behavior?\n- Are hook dependency arrays correct? Missing deps cause stale closures; extra deps cause infinite loops.\n- If this component unmounts mid-async-operation, is cleanup handled?\n\nOnly report if you can trace a specific input that triggers the bug. Do not report theoretical concerns.\n\n**If no checks produced a potential finding, stop and report zero findings. Do not invent issues to fill the report. An empty result is the correct output when the code has no bugs matching these patterns.**\n\nEach code location should be reported once under the most specific matching pattern. Do not flag the same line under multiple checks.\n\n## Step 3: Report Findings\n\nFor each finding, include:\n\n- **Title**: Short description of the bug\n- **Severity**: high, medium, or low\n- **Location**: File path and line number\n- **Description**: Root cause → consequences (2-4 sentences)\n- **Precedent**: A real production issue ID (e.g., \"Similar to JAVASCRIPT-2NQW: null charCodeAt in SQL parser, 39K events\")\n- **Fix**: A unified diff showing the code fix\n\nFix suggestions must include actual code. Never suggest a comment or docstring as a fix.\n\nDo not prescribe your own output format — the review harness controls the response structure.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:26:20.746Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing advanced JavaScript frontend bug detection and performance monitoring capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级JavaScript前端bug检测和性能监控功能的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが高度なJavaScriptフロントエンドバグ検出とパフォーマンス監視機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 JavaScript 프런트엔드 버그 탐지 및 성능 모니터링 기능이 필요한 코드 검토 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de detección de errores y monitoreo de rendimiento de frontend de JavaScript.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant des capacités avancées de détection d''erreurs et de surveillance des performances de frontend JavaScript.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die erweiterte JavaScript-Frontend-Fehlererkennungs- und Leistungsüberwachungsfähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de detecção avançada de bugs de frontend em JavaScript e capacidades de monitoramento de desempenho.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов проверки кода, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности обнаружения ошибок frontend на JavaScript и мониторинга производительности.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى كشف متقدم عن أخطاء الجافا سكريبت في واجهة المستخدم وسمات مراقبة الأداء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify and resolve real production errors in Sentry frontend code by checking for patterns that cause over 524,000 error events, utilizing knowledge from 428 resolved, ignored, and unresolved issues, and leveraging developer-first error tracking and performance monitoring protocols.","zh":"赋予代理识别和解决真实生产错误的Sentry前端代码中的问题，通过检查导致超过524,000个错误事件的模式，利用428个已解决、忽略和未解决问题的知识，并利用开发者优先的错误跟踪和性能监控协议。","ja":"エージェントが実際のプロダクションエラーを識別および解決できるようにすることで、Sentryフロントエンドコード内の問題を解決します。524,000を超えるエラーイベントを引き起こすパターンをチェックし、428の解決済み、無視された、および解決されていない問題からの知識を利用し、開発者ファーストのエラートラッキングおよびパフォーマンスモニタリングプロトコルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 실제 프로덕션 오류를 식별 및 해결할 수 있도록 해주는 Sentry 프론트엔드 코드에서 문제를 해결합니다. 524,000개를 초과하는 오류 이벤트를 유발하는 패턴을 확인하고, 428개의 해결된, 무시된, 해결되지 않은 문제에서 얻은 지식을 활용하며, 개발자 우선의 오류 추적 및 성능 모니터링 규약을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar y resolver errores reales de producción en el código frontend de Sentry, comprobando patrones que causan más de 524.000 eventos de error, utilizando conocimientos de 428 problemas resueltos, ignorados y no resueltos, y aprovechando protocolos de seguimiento de errores y monitoreo de rendimiento orientados al desarrollador.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier et de résoudre les véritables erreurs de production dans le code frontend de Sentry, en vérifiant les modèles qui provoquent plus de 524 000 événements d''erreur, en utilisant les connaissances de 428 problèmes résolus, ignorés et non résolus, et en exploitant les protocoles de suivi d''erreurs et de surveillance des performances axés sur le développeur.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, reale Produktionsfehler im Sentry-Frontend-Code zu identifizieren und zu lösen, indem sie Muster überprüfen, die mehr als 524.000 Fehlerereignisse verursachen, und dabei Wissen aus 428 behobenen, ignorierten und unbehebten Problemen nutzen und entwicklerorientierte Fehlerverfolgungs- und Leistungsüberwachungsprotokolle nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar e resolver erros reais de produção no código frontend do Sentry, verificando padrões que causam mais de 524.000 eventos de erro, utilizando conhecimento de 428 problemas resolvidos, ignorados e não resolvidos, e aproveitando protocolos de rastreamento de erros e monitoramento de desempenho orientados ao desenvolvedor.","ru":"Позволяет агентам выявлять и решать реальные ошибки производства в коде frontend Sentry, проверяя закономерности, которые вызывают более 524 000 событий ошибок, используя знания из 428 решенных, проигнорированных и нерешенных проблем, и используя протоколы отслеживания ошибок и мониторинга производительности, ориентированные на разработчика.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تحديد ومعالجة أخطاء الإنتاج الفعلية في код واجهة المستخدم في سيتري من خلال التحقق من الأنماط التي تسبب أكثر من 524000 حدث خطأ، باستخدام المعرفة من 428 مشكلة محلولة ومُهملة و未 محلولة، واستخدام بروتوكولات تتبع الأخطاء ومراقبة الأداء الموجهة للمطور."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging Sentry JavaScript frontend code for production errors","Analyzing scoped code chunks from Warden''s diff for bug patterns","Resolving issues based on known fixes from resolved production issues"],"zh":["调试Sentry JavaScript前端代码以查找生产错误","分析Warden的diff中的范围代码块以查找bug模式","根据已解决的生产问题中的已知修复来解决问题"],"ja":["プロダクションエラーのためにSentry JavaScriptフロントエンドコードをデバッグする","Wardenのdiff内のスコープコードチャンクをバグパターンに分析する","解決済みのプロダクション問題からの既知の修正に基づいて問題を解決する"],"ko":["생산 오류에 대한 Sentry JavaScript 프론트엔드 코드를 디버깅하는 것","Warden의 diff 내의 범위 코드 조각을 버그 패턴으로 분석하는 것","해결된 프로덕션 문제에서 알려진 수정 사항을 기반으로 문제를 해결하는 것"],"es":["Depuración del código frontend de JavaScript de Sentry para errores de producción","Análisis de trozos de código con alcance desde la diferencia de Warden para patrones de errores","Resolución de problemas en función de soluciones conocidas de problemas de producción resueltos"],"fr":["Débogage du code frontend JavaScript de Sentry pour les erreurs de production","Analyse de morceaux de code à portée depuis la différence de Warden pour les modèles d''erreurs","Résolution de problèmes en fonction de corrections connues de problèmes de production résolus"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung im Sentry-JavaScript-Frontend-Code für Produktionsfehler","Analyse von Code-Stücken mit Umfang aus Warden''s Diff für Fehlermuster","Behebung von Problemen basierend auf bekannten Lösungen für behobene Produktionsprobleme"],"pt":["Depuração do código frontend do Sentry em JavaScript para erros de produção","Análise de pedaços de código com escopo do diff do Warden para padrões de bugs","Resolução de problemas com base em soluções conhecidas de problemas de produção resolvidos"],"ru":["Отладка кода frontend Sentry на JavaScript для ошибок производства","Анализ фрагментов кода из diff Warden для закономерностей ошибок","Решение проблем на основе известных исправлений решенных проблем производства"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء الشفرة الجافا سكريبت في واجهة المستخدم في سيتري للأخطاء الإنتاجية","تحليل شذرات الشفرة المحددة النطاق من diff واردين للأنماط الخطأ","معالجة المشكلات بناءً على الإصلاحات المعروفة للمشكلات الإنتاجية المحلولة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to Sentry frontend code and Warden''s diff","Limited to JavaScript frontend bug detection and performance monitoring"],"zh":["需要访问Sentry前端代码和Warden的diff","仅限于JavaScript前端bug检测和性能监控"],"ja":["SentryフロントエンドコードおよびWardenのdiffへのアクセスが必要","JavaScriptフロントエンドバグ検出およびパフォーマンスモニタリングのみ"],"ko":["Sentry 프론트엔드 코드 및 Warden의 diff에 대한 액세스가 필요함","JavaScript 프론트엔드 버그 감지 및 성능 모니터링만"],"es":["Requiere acceso al código frontend de Sentry y a la diferencia de Warden","Limitado a la detección de errores y monitoreo de rendimiento de frontend de JavaScript"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès au code frontend de Sentry et à la différence de Warden","Limité à la détection d''erreurs et à la surveillance des performances de frontend JavaScript"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf den Sentry-Frontend-Code und Warden''s Diff","Begrenzt auf die Fehlererkennung und Leistungsüberwachung von JavaScript-Frontend"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao código frontend do Sentry e ao diff do Warden","Limitado à detecção de bugs de frontend em JavaScript e monitoramento de desempenho"],"ru":["Требует доступа к коду frontend Sentry и diff Warden","Ограничен обнаружением ошибок frontend на JavaScript и мониторингом производительности"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى شفرة واجهة المستخدم في سيتري و diff واردين","محدود بكشف أخطاء الجافا سكريبت في واجهة المستخدم ومراقبة الأداء"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"d07bf794068b15cb425aee44b7bc3f405fec4b5a1a376346254d70651461e4f3","qualityScore":40}');
